 Williams II, archaeologists discovered a rectangular stone across the front of the stadium [1]. This is thought to be the starting line [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94430", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94431", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-1500'' -> ''-400''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143994", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-004: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d0/Stadium_of_Nemea_in_2004%2C_Neme451.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1bc57ad9/Inside the Stadium of Nemea on October 31, 2019.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:307767", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1bc57ad9/Inside the Stadium of Nemea on October 31, 2019.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1bc57ad9/Stadium_of_Nemea_in_2004,_Neme451.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
