orated interior spaces. A devastating earthquake at the end of the 13th century BC destroyed the citadel, leaving a crushed human skeleton among the ruins. The rich necropolis at neighboring Dendra further attests to its significance.'' -> ''One of the three main Mycenaean centers in the Argolid alongside Mycenae and Tiryns, situated on a 270-meter conical hill [1] [2] [3]. Its massive cyclopean wall extends 450 meters in length, stands 5-7 meters wide, and survives up to 7 meters high in places [1] [2] [4]. The rich necropolis at neighboring Dendra further attests to its significance [5].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309564", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3b7fc9a8/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3b7fc9a8/Midea.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
